{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "93504f8f-62b0-4fec-8e88-787d8b084dbe",
    "name": "PAD Team 2 \u2014 Exam Service",
    "description": "Exam Service (Gurschi Gheorghe, Go). Owns exam definitions, the question bank, attempts, scores, academic progress and achievements.\n\n**Running it:** start the service with `go run ./cmd/server` in this repository, then run the whole collection. Every request asserts the status code the contract promises, so a green run means the service still honours it.\n\n**Data:** the service seeds two courses at boot, `math_analysis` and `operating_systems`. The CRUD folders create and delete their own throwaway records and the exam flow generates a fresh player on every run, so the collection can be run repeatedly.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Exam flow",
      "description": "The sequence the Game Service drives when a player meets a Professor Zombie. Run in order.\n\nThe first request generates a fresh player and encounter id, so the folder can be run repeatedly without colliding with attempts left behind by the previous run.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Start an attempt",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/exams/attempts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "exams",
                "attempts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Starts an exam for a player who met a Professor Zombie. Called by the Game Service.\n\nIdempotent by `encounter_id`: a retry after a timeout returns the existing attempt with **200** instead of creating a second one. A fresh encounter returns **201**.\n\nErrors: 404 when the course has no questions, 409 when the player already has an attempt in progress.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"player_id\": \"{{playerId}}\",\n  \"game_session_id\": \"session-1\",\n  \"encounter_id\": \"{{encounterId}}\",\n  \"course_id\": \"{{courseId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh player and encounter per run, so the collection stays re-runnable.",
                  "const run = Date.now();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"playerId\", \"player-\" + run);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"encounterId\", \"enc-\" + run);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"spareEncounterId\", \"enc-\" + run + \"-spare\");"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"responds 201\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (pm.response.code < 300) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"attemptId\", pm.response.json().attempt_id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Start it again \u2014 same encounter",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/exams/attempts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "exams",
                "attempts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The same `encounter_id` as the previous request. Proves the idempotency: the response carries the same `attempt_id` and the status is 200, not 201.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"player_id\": \"{{playerId}}\",\n  \"game_session_id\": \"session-1\",\n  \"encounter_id\": \"{{encounterId}}\",\n  \"course_id\": \"{{courseId}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"responds 200\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"returns the same attempt\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().attempt_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"attemptId\"));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
